            <div xml:id="d921">

                <pb facs="1037" n="1025" sameAs="frus:frus1943v03/pg1025"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115A Pacific War/486: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-22">June 22,
                        1943</date>.<lb/>[Received June 23—2:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3716. American interests Japan. Department’s 1255 of May 25th. Consulate,
                    Shanghai, telegraphs: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Japanese authorities now permit monthly payments interned civilians in
                            form pocket money.</p>
                        <pb facs="1038" n="1026" xml:id="pg1026"/>
                        <p>Have decided for present allocate 700 Nanking dollars to internees,
                            equivalent about 40 Swiss francs per person monthly because
                            insufficiency food at camps and constant depreciation currency. This
                            amount probably soon requires increase.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
